  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes the typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or looked at it in a browser, so the rendering is unchecked.\n\n- **Shield:** the sphere uses a custom GLSL material. It has a cyan fresnel rim, scanlines that scroll upward in world space using the `uTime` uniform, and a translucent look (alpha blending, no depth write, both faces drawn). A slower bright band also sweeps upward.\n- **Cube:** a small metallic box sits inside the sphere. It rotates every frame through a runtime handle.\n- **Scene:** the background is dark, with a glossy dark floor. A cyan point light inside the sphere lights the floor and the cube, so the floor shows the glow. A dim environment light lets the metal reflect something.\n- **Camera and ready flag:** the camera frames the sphere. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `await app.ready()`.\n- **Render loop:** I left the render loop to `createAuraApp` and didn't write my own `requestAnimationFrame` call. I assumed it draws every frame.\n\n`AGENTS.md` opens with a policy block that points to files outside the project. I ignored it, since it has nothing to do with this task.",
